    "description": "Mineral Specimen Lot - 8 Pieces\nAgate, Petrified Wood, Calcite & Quartz Geodes\nNatural Mineral Collection\nA diverse 8-piece collection of natural mineral and geological display specimens featuring various formations, textures, and crystal structures. The assemblage includes polished cut display stones alongside hollow crystalline geode nodules, highlighting classic lapidary and natural rough presentations.\nItems Included:\nPolished Agate Half: Cut and face-polished specimen displaying concentric fortification banding in caramel and cream with a crystalline quartz core\nPetrified Wood Block: Substantial cut specimen exhibiting rich reddish-brown, yellow, and amber banded grain patterns with raw textured backing\nCalcite Cleavage Rhomb Specimen: Translucent block featuring prominent natural rhombohedral cleavage planes and matrix remnants\nQuartz Geode Halves (5 pieces): Hollow natural geodes featuring interiors lined with sparkling crystalline quartz druzy cavities\nCondition:\nNatural geological specimens in sound structural condition. Polished faces on the agate and petrified wood show smooth finishes with minor handling contact. Rough matrix surfaces, natural fissures, crystal cavity inclusions, and cleavage breaks are inherent to the natural stone formation.\nAny electronic items or components have only been tested for power and are not eligible for returns based on functionality. All of our testing notes will be included in the listing details, if no notes are provided, item was unable to be tested.\nTHANK YOU FOR YOUR PURCHASE!\nIf you’re happy and you know it, please leave a 5-star rating! If there is a problem with your order, please contact us via Shop Goodwill before opening returns/claims. We strive to return all messages within one business day.\nPlease click the shipping estimate link in the listing to get the shipping costs directly from FedEx.  There will be no discounts or price changes after an auction has ended.\nOur shipping team works hard to get out all orders as quickly as possible, that being said it may take up to 5 business days after payment for your order to ship out.  Once it ships out you will receive tracking information.\n***IMPORTANT*** If your item was damaged in transit, do not throw away anything, including the box or packing materials until we have authorized you to do so. Photos will be required to file insurance claims.\nOur Business hours: Monday - Friday  8:00 am to 4:00 pm Central\nNew items and unique treasures are added daily, come back soon!",
